    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nThis fixes the `live_grep` behavior when `ignorecase` is enabled. Previously, searching for `todo` in this file would **only** match the lowercase line:\r\n```\r\n// TODO: fix this\r\n// todo: fix this\r\n```\r\n\r\nPS: had a couple of tests in `test_pick` fail on me, but this was also the case prior to my PR. Not sure what to do about that.\r\n\r\nPS: love your plugins man. <3",
    "closed_at": "2024-12-19T11:09:45Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nThe current `rg` command line arguments are picked as smallest set possible to have a working grep. Making `live_grep` respect 'ingorecase'/'smartcase' (as other \"regular\" pickers do) was considered before, but it introduces issues.\r\n\r\nThe problem with adding more arguments is that they will override user's config for `rg` itself. I can imagine that there might be the case of having different preferences for `live_grep` and Neovim's searching when it comes to ignoring case.\r\n\r\nSo my suggestion here would be to [create `rg` config](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-pick.txt#L80-L85) and set this argument there. This way it will be respected on \"per config\" basis instead of forcing arguments based on Neovim's options. I personally [use this approach](https://github.com/echasnovski/dotfiles/blob/master/ripgrep/.config/ripgrep/.ripgreprc) (don't forget to `export RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH=\"$HOME/.config/ripgrep/.ripgreprc\"` with config path of your choice).",
